      <Comment source="PMN, zhang, SRI, caspi">|FRAME: CPD-14133| is a hydrated form of |FRAME: NADPH|, where the hydroxyl group is attached at position 6 of the nicotinamide moiety in (&lt;i&gt;R&lt;/i&gt;) configuration. NAD(P)H spontaneously hydrates to both the (6S)- and (6R)- isomers, and these are interconverted by |FRAME: EC-5.1.99.6|, to a 60:40 ratio |CITS: [21994945]|.</Comment>
